flowchart TD
  A[Entry] --> B[View overview]
  B --> C{Choose action}
  C --> D[Edit or configure]
  C --> E[Review details]
  D --> F{Valid state?}
  F -->|No| G[Show local correction]
  G --> D
  F -->|Yes| H[Confirm change]
  H --> I[Show completed state]
  E --> J[Return to overview]
  I --> J
  J --> B

Rationale: The path covers orientation, action, validation, confirmation, completion, and return.
Quality gates: each action has a destination; invalid states have local guidance; completion differs from progress; return is available.
Repository intent: /projects/project-001/sections/h/flows.mmd is the canonical interaction narrative.
Writing rule: use short neutral verbs and one outcome per node.
Publishing rule: publish only when node names match the state matrix and responsive behavior is documented.